# Go
#   Go keeps its build and module caches in the user profile, so the project
#   tree stays clean on its own. What's left is compiled output, test
#   artifacts, and the local workspace file.

# Compiled output
#   `go build` drops the binary next to the source unless pointed elsewhere;
#   bin/ covers the conventional -o target.
bin/
*.exe

# Test and profiling artifacts
#   *.test comes from `go test -c`, *.out from coverage and pprof.
*.test
*.out

# Go workspace file
#   go.work is a local multi-module convenience; committing it imposes your
#   directory layout on everyone else.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Dependencies
#   go.sum is deliberately NOT ignored, it is the lockfile. vendor/ is also
#   not ignored: if you vendor at all, the committed copy is the point.

# Environment files
.env

# IntelliJ
.idea/
